{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Stdlib.Type</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"melange","href":"../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Stdlib","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Type","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[{"title":"Type equality witness","href":"#witness","children":[]},{"title":"Type identifiers","href":"#identifiers","children":[]}],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Type introspection.</p><ul class=\"at-tags\"><li class=\"since\"><span class=\"at-tag\">since</span> 5.1</li></ul>","content":"<h2 id=\"witness\"><a href=\"#witness\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Type equality witness</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-eq\"><a href=\"#type-eq\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> eq(_, _)</span><span> = </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-eq.Equal\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-eq.Equal\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span><span class=\"constructor\">Equal</span> : <a href=\"#type-eq\">eq</a><span>(<span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>, <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span></span></code></li></ol><code><span>;</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The purpose of <code>eq</code> is to represent type equalities that may not otherwise be known by the type checker (e.g. because they may depend on dynamic data).</p><p>A value of type <code>(a, b) eq</code> represents the fact that types <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> are equal.</p><p>If one has a value <code>eq : (a, b) eq</code> that proves types <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> are equal, one can use it to convert a value of type <code>a</code> to a value of type <code>b</code> by pattern matching on <code>Equal</code>:</p><pre class=\"language-ocaml\"><code>  let cast (type a) (type b) (Equal : (a, b) Type.eq) (a : a) : b = a</code></pre><p>At runtime, this function simply returns its second argument unchanged.</p></div></div><h2 id=\"identifiers\"><a href=\"#identifiers\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Type identifiers</h2><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Id\"><a href=\"#module-Id\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Id/index.html\">Id</a></span><span>: { ... }</span><span>;</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Type identifiers.</p></div></div>"}